1
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Lost at Sea: The Search for Longitude is a adventure,
documentary, drama film directed by Peter Jones.

2
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:18,000
It was one of humankind's most epic quests - a technical problem so complex that it challenged the best minds of
its time, a problem so important that the nation that solved it would rule the economy of the world.

3
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:54,000
The problem was navigation by sea—how to know where you were when you
sailed beyond the sight of land - establishing your longitude.

4
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,000
While the gentry of the 18th Century looked to the stars for the answer, an English
clockmaker, John Harrison, toiled for decades to solve the problem.

5
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
His elegant solution made him an unlikely hero and remains the basis for
the most modern forms of navigation in the world today.

6
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:42,000
This film will be both a celebration of Harrison's
invention and an adventure story.

7
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:18,000
An expedition on a period sailing vessel as it sails the open sea will demonstrate
the life and death importance of finding your longitude at sea.

8
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Narrator, played by Richard Dreyfuss.

9
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:30,000
John Harrison, played by Patrick Malahide.

10
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Longitude: The True Story of a Lone Genius Who Solved the Greatest Scientific Problem of His Time is a 1995 best-selling book by Dava Sobel about John Harrison, an
18th-century clockmaker who created the first clock (chronometer) sufficiently accurate to be used to determine longitude at sea—an important development in navigation.

11
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
The book was made into a television series entitled Longitude.

12
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
In 1998, The Illustrated Longitude was published, supplementing the earlier text with
180 images of characters, events, instruments, maps and publications.

13
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:54,000
The film explores themes of biography, docudrama, navigation.

14
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
